 "description": "Doug's homemade capybara suit (worn prop over the 'stand' pose; anchor = Doug's hips, list after Doug at the same x/y/scale). Brown felt #9a6a3a barrel suit from the shoulders (y -154) to the knees (y +82) with tacking stitches, a patch and a safety pin, stubby felt legs to y +110 (Doug's shins show below), stubby paw mitts at the sides; a blunt felt capybara snout (button eyes, nostril, two cream incisors) sticking out forward at x 66..210, y -220..-144, right under the red cap brim like a second brim, tied back with a string under the chin line; a small hood flap with two little ears behind the head (x < -50). Doug's face and the whole cap stay visible. No antlers. ~330x360.",
